1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,720
Part two:

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:04,886
public financial management in India.

3
00:00:06,436 --> 00:00:08,207
PFM is a set of processes.

4
00:00:08,257 --> 00:00:12,828
A government forecasts and tracks the
funds it raises or receives.

5
00:00:12,878 --> 00:00:18,219
It decides how they will be spent, across
multiple tiers and many ministries,

6
00:00:18,269 --> 00:00:19,900
departments and schemes.

7
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:23,611
It tracks the transfer of funds until they
are spent.

8
00:00:23,661 --> 00:00:27,532
And it tracks the outputs and outcomes of
that spending.

9
00:00:27,582 --> 00:00:31,383
Around this sit compliance, the quality of
expenditure,

10
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:33,554
and prudent management of debt.

11
00:00:35,104 --> 00:00:37,021
The lifecycle has four phases:

12
00:00:37,071 --> 00:00:41,153
budget formulation, legislative approval,
execution, and audit.

13
00:00:41,203 --> 00:00:45,087
Because budgeting is an annual exercise,
the phases overlap:

14
00:00:45,137 --> 00:00:50,530
this year's budget is prepared while last
year's is executed and the year before is

15
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:51,055
audited.

16
00:00:51,105 --> 00:00:55,055
That is why one budget speech presents
three sets of figures:

17
00:00:55,105 --> 00:01:00,105
budget estimates for the coming year,
revised estimates for the ongoing year,

18
00:01:00,155 --> 00:01:02,990
and the audited actuals for the year
before.

19
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,656
PFM happens across four tiers.

20
00:01:06,706 --> 00:01:11,278
The Union and the States, each with a
legislature, an executive,

21
00:01:11,328 --> 00:01:13,517
and constitutional authorities.

22
00:01:13,567 --> 00:01:18,860
Around seven hundred and fifty districts,
where many schemes are executed.

23
00:01:18,910 --> 00:01:22,760
And local governments, the third tier
created in 1992.

24
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:25,649
Two more actors matter during execution:

25
00:01:25,699 --> 00:01:31,570
the vendors whose services government procures,
and the banks that move the money.

26
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:36,986
All of it is governed by the General
Financial Rules, first issued in 1947.

27
00:01:38,536 --> 00:01:42,337
Local governments depend heavily on
Finance Commission grants.

28
00:01:42,387 --> 00:01:47,244
The fourteenth commission allocated about
two hundred and eighty-eight thousand

29
00:01:47,294 --> 00:01:49,045
crore rupees over five years.

30
00:01:49,095 --> 00:01:53,890
The fifteenth raised that to about four
hundred and thirty-six thousand crore,

31
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:55,132
fifty per cent more.

32
00:01:55,182 --> 00:01:57,119
The grants come with conditions:

33
00:01:57,169 --> 00:02:00,535
state finance commissions in place,
published accounts,

34
00:02:00,585 --> 00:02:05,318
and property tax collections that grow at
least as fast as the state economy.

35
00:02:06,868 --> 00:02:08,742
Digitisation has gone far.

36
00:02:08,792 --> 00:02:14,366
The Public Financial Management System,
PFMS, connects every state treasury,

37
00:02:14,416 --> 00:02:19,028
over three hundred banks, and around fifty
beneficiary systems.

38
00:02:19,078 --> 00:02:25,170
The Single Nodal Agency reform of 2021 stops
funds being parked unspent across many

39
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:25,836
accounts.

40
00:02:25,886 --> 00:02:30,720
And state integrated financial management
systems handle payments,

41
00:02:30,770 --> 00:02:32,570
reporting and monitoring.

42
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:40,077
Take any large scheme, such as MGNREGS,
the National Health Mission, or PM-KISAN.

43
00:02:40,127 --> 00:02:43,266
The Union approves, allocates and
releases.

44
00:02:43,316 --> 00:02:48,087
The State consolidates proposals, demands
funds and manages them.

45
00:02:48,137 --> 00:02:52,834
Districts and blocks consolidate
activities and monitor budgets.

46
00:02:52,884 --> 00:02:56,764
Local bodies prepare proposals and
beneficiary lists.

47
00:02:56,814 --> 00:03:02,030
Every scheme is a chain of hand-offs
across tiers, and so is its money.

48
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:04,367
Next:

49
00:03:04,417 --> 00:03:08,396
the challenges, and the pivotal problem
behind them.
